<h3 id="use-case">Use Case</h3>

<p>Recently I’ve been developing a plugin and need to copy the plugin from the project directory to the system plugin directory <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">~/Library/Internet Plug-Ins/</code> (here I’m using Lao Tan’s plugin as an example: <a href="http://www.tanhao.me/pieces/1084.html/">here</a>)</p>

<p>As shown below:
<img src="/assets/images/20170509HowToCreateSymbolicLinkOnMacosInCode/step1.avif" alt="step" /></p>

<p>I originally wanted to copy it directly, but there might be upgrade issues in the future, and then handling the logic of judging versions and deleting old ones would be troublesome. So I thought of using an alias instead.</p>

<p><img src="/assets/images/20170509HowToCreateSymbolicLinkOnMacosInCode/step2.avif" alt="step" /></p>

<p>Create the alias using this approach:</p>

<div class="language-objc highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code><table class="rouge-table"><tbody><tr><!-- <td class="rouge-gutter gl"><pre class="lineno">1
